2024-01-15 | TRACKER: Chose ByteTrack via ultralytics over DeepSORT — no re-ID model needed, keeps Docker image small, satisfies zero-manual-steps gate.
2024-01-15 | SCHEMA: Session is unit of measure (not raw event count) — REENTRY and staff filtering require per-visitor state that raw counts cannot express.
2024-01-15 | STORAGE: SQLiteRepo behind Repo interface — zero-infra for Docker gate, single-file swap to Postgres, tmp_path injection for test isolation.
2024-01-15 | POS: IST→UTC conversion done once at load_and_process_pos boundary — prevents off-by-5h30m bugs in all downstream correlation logic.
2024-01-15 | HTTP: Return 207 (not 422) for partial ingest failures — bad events are business-data errors; callers receive partial results rather than a hard rejection.
2026-06-02 | EC-13 (3-SECOND TRAP): Appearance similarity is the SOLE arbiter of re-entry; timing only prunes the gallery window. reentry_decision() was designed this way because two different people can enter 3 seconds apart — timing tells us nothing about identity.
2026-06-02 | EC-1 (GROUP ENTRY): EntryExitCounter uses per-track debounce dict, not per-blob. 8px hysteresis band prevents doorway oscillation from generating phantom events.
2026-06-02 | EC-16 (LOST TRACK): LostTrackBuffer TTL=45 frames (~1.5s at 30fps) — enough time to stitch tracks behind a display unit without absorbing new people who enter the same area.
2026-06-02 | EC-17 (CROSS-CAM): ReIDGallery shared across all cameras; crosscam_inherit called before assigning new visitor_id — ensures one person crossing camera boundaries keeps one session, not two.
2026-06-02 | EC-20 (STICKY STAFF): lock_conf=0.8 chosen — below this, a staff member might be misclassified by lighting; above this, we lock forever so subsequent frames with poor angle don't flip the label.
2026-06-02 | DASHBOARD: Professional ops tool, two views only (Live Operations / Store Report). Purplle brand palette (#C8006B, #1A1A2E, #F3EDF7). DM Sans matches Purplle consumer app. Every element answers one of: conversion rate, active alerts, zone attention vs revenue.
2026-06-02 | EC-35 (MULTI-ITEM BASKET): baskets_from_pos groups by invoice_number — Brigade CSV yields exactly 24 baskets from 101 line items. The #1 failure mode this challenge tests for. Test asserts the literal count.
2026-06-02 | EC-49 (IST→UTC): pos_local_to_utc is the ONLY place IST is converted to UTC. A 5h30m off-by-default silently zeros all POS correlation; placing conversion at the load boundary eliminates the class of bug.
2026-06-02 | EC-36 (GUEST CHECKOUT): "Guest" is NEVER a usable identity — different physical people share the name. Conversion correlation uses ONLY the time-window + billing-zone match, never customer_name.
2026-06-02 | EC-37 (UNIQUE BUYERS): Each Guest counts as 1 unique buyer; named customers dedup by case-normalised name. We do NOT merge anonymous baskets — that would underreport buyers.
2026-06-02 | EC-38 (MOBILE POS FALLBACK): If no billing-zone session matches a transaction within the window, fall back to last-zone exit-time. Catches transactions made via salesperson mobile POS (no billing camera appearance).
2026-06-02 | EC-42 (CLOCK SKEW): Estimate offset by cross-correlating billing-event and POS-txn minute histograms. Maximum product-sum identifies the shift. Avoids hard-coded clock-sync assumption.
2026-06-02 | FUNNEL DEDUP: Each stage uses set(visitor_id), never event counts. Stage N's set is the intersection of all prior stages — monotonic decrease is enforced via assert, REENTRY can't double-count.
2026-06-02 | BRAND HEATMAP: zone_brand_map config inverts to {normalised_brand: zone_id}. POS revenue per brand is summed into zone_revenue. Reveals Purplle's specific value — DERMdoc shows 86% sales_share / 0% dwell_share = needs camera coverage, not re-merchandising.
2026-06-02 | DEAD_ZONE vs COVERAGE_GAP: Distinct anomaly types. DEAD_ZONE = covered zone with zero visits (merchandising problem). COVERAGE_GAP = uncovered zone (telemetry gap). Misclassifying these would tell a manager "fix the camera" when they should "rethink the placement".
2026-06-02 | CONVERSION_DROP BASELINE: 7-day rolling average from daily_stats (SQLite). Fires only when today < 60% of baseline AND visitors ≥ 20 AND baseline exists. Placeholder threshold removed — this is now a real signal.
2026-06-02 | STRUCTURED LOGGING: One JSON line per request. trace_id is a UUID4, attached to request.state, returned in X-Trace-Id header. Unhandled exceptions return HTTP 503 with {error, trace_id, message} — never expose stack trace.
2026-06-02 | STALE_FEED: lag > 600s flags STALE_FEED per store. Service status stays "ok" so the health endpoint itself remains queryable when a feed dies.
2026-06-02 | EC-50 (CONFIDENCE BANDS): HIGH ≥0.7, MEDIUM ≥0.4, LOW <0.4. session_confidence_distribution exposed in /metrics and /funnel so operators see how much of today's data is reliable.
2026-06-02 | DASHBOARD ALIAS: GET /dashboard/ mirrors GET / so the spec's URL works AND the root URL works. One html template, two routes, zero duplicated logic.
2026-06-02 | SSE 2s INTERVAL: /dashboard/stream/{store_id} emits every 2 seconds (not 1, not 5). 1s is wasted CPU on a metric that changes per-event-batch (≈10s cadence at busy hour). 5s feels stale on a live demo. 2s is the demo-correct interval.
2026-06-02 | TEST PROMPT/CHANGES BLOCKS: Every test file documents one place I overrode AI output. These become demo answers — when a reviewer asks "show me one thing the AI got wrong", I open the test header. The blocks are real corrections, not placeholders.
2026-06-02 | ZONE OWNERSHIP: Each zone has exactly one camera in camera_zone_ownership. Cross-camera overlap zones (LAKME visible from both CAM_01 and CAM_02 angles) generate events ONLY from the owning camera. This is EC-18 — prevents double-counting at the data layer instead of trying to dedup downstream.
2026-06-02 | SUBMISSION TAG: v1.0-submission. Tests 144/144 green. Coverage 69% overall, every business module ≥78%. Acceptance gate verified live: /, /dashboard/, /health, /events/ingest, /stores/:id/metrics, /funnel, /heatmap, /anomalies all return valid JSON with no manual steps after docker compose up.
